Z||000000||Fiasco||05-15-2000||01:41 AM||||Maybe a dumb question, but should the dash vents shut off completely? In my 85, it seems there is always air coming in the vents regardless of the lever positions. It does get warmer or colder like it should, but even with the fan in the off position, I have to shut the vents individually. -Is this normal or do I have a stuck flap somewhere???<BR>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||05-15-2000||11:34 AM||||The dash controls, the control motor behind the radio or one of the linkages has a problem. Quick test is sub the controls.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||05-15-2000||02:10 PM||||If you can believe the diagram on the last page of the Haynes manual it shows that all of the baffle doors have a gap by design. That would allow a "little" air to pass reguardless of door position.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-15-2000||03:54 PM||||The defog will always flow a little bit. The dash vents usually shut off all the way on most things. Is it s little bit or is it blowing like it normally would on vent? If it's a little bit then it's may be intentional. If it's allot then it's definatly not normal.||||reg||1
